# (build 97c) The rocky mountain on Motavia: ObjType_Events $2B
# (loc_DF24, ps2.asm:20444), an event block (object $38) at 2768,1544 --
# cell 173,96. A on it opens the small message box (loc_D84A) and loads
# $171F; $DE72 + 1, so the next button closes the box (ObjType_Events'
# first test); loc_DDA2 names {char}. The script is cut short in the ROM:
# its first page ends in $C4 ("; this should be $C3" in the disassembly),
# and LoadScript ends a script at any code $C4 and up (loc_11268), so
# only "There is a high rocky mountain in front of" is ever shown -- the
# second page, "{char} and the others! Is this Uzo mountain?", is never
# loaded. The port does the same. Before build 97c the port had no case
# for the event: A there was "There seems to be nothing unusual here."
# ($1708, people line 0).
#
# It is on Uzo's island: from the cell below the mountain (173,97, the
# door record) a step up is Uzo's entrance, but one cell to the left the
# mountain only turns the party (172,97 facing up), and A there hits the
# event block.

start slot 1 routes/saves/jet_scooter.json
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen level
wait idle
expect level 0 89 116
warp 0 172 97
wait screen level
wait idle
press up                     # the mountain: a turn, no step
wait idle
expect level 0 172 97
press a
wait idle
expect script $171F
shot 01_mountain
press c                      # the box closes: there is no second page
wait idle
expect level 0 172 97
